        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A tankless water heater is a simple idea executed with a lot of firepower: heat the water as it moves instead of keeping a tank of it hot all day. That gives you hot water that never runs out, a unit that lasts around twice as long as a tank, and lower standby losses, in exchange for a fixed limit on flow and a more involved installation.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whether it works in your house comes down to two numbers, your peak flow and your winter temperature rise, plus the gas, venting or electrical capacity to feed the unit. Get those right and a tankless heater is one of the better upgrades a home can make. Get them wrong and it is an expensive way to have lukewarm showers.
          </p>
        </div>

